# Data and leakage

- Persist every API pull as a timestamped snapshot. A row is usable for gameweek N only if captured before that GW deadline.
- Shift all rolling match stats by at least one match within each player. Same-GW `minutes`, `starts`, `goals`, `xG`, `defensive_contribution`, and `total_points` are labels, not features.
- Treat FPL `ep_this` / `ep_next` and vaastav `xP` as leak-prone. Use them only from pre-deadline snapshots. Missing projection = `-1`, never `0`.
- Player IDs are not stable across FPL / Understat / FBref / football-data.co.uk. Maintain an explicit mapping table and fail rows that do not join cleanly.
- Rate-limit `element-summary/{id}/` (hundreds of calls). Cache per run; do not hammer the API.
- Historical scoring changed in 2025/26 (defensive contribution). Tag seasons with a ruleset id; do not mix eras in one unadjusted target.
